<TSL-SYSTEM Terminal> $music, A command which searches and plays music from the internet.
Usage: music [play|stop|pause] [INDEX/KEYWORD]
       music search KEYWORD
       music get INDEX/KEYWORD

Crawl the public music library on the internet, download the selected
music to the local tools/Music/Musics directory, and play the local music
in the background. The playback is handled by the mother system, so the
terminal
is never blocked and other commands can still be executed while music is
playing. The playback state is shared by all TSL-SYSTEM processes, so
another terminal window can also pause or stop the playing music.

Command Options:
    play,             Start the background playback, or resume it if paused.
                      If INDEX/KEYWORD is given, the matched local music is
                      played immediately.
    stop,             Stop the background playback.
    pause,            Pause the background playback, or resume it if paused.
    search,           Crawl the internet and list the matched music. The
                      result is numbered and kept for 'music get'.
    get,              Download the selected music to the local
                      tools/Music/Musics directory. INDEX is the number of
                      the result of 'music search', and KEYWORD crawls the
                      internet again.

Examples:
    music
    music search 晴天
    music get 1
    music get hello adele
    music play
    music play 3
    music pause
    music stop

The crawler supports the netease and kugou sources. Because of the
copyright restriction, some music can only be searched as a cover or a
sample, and downloading it fails with a CrawlerError message; choose
another result in that case.

Music files are downloaded to and searched in the tools/Music/Musics
directory of TSL-SYSTEM. Use 'execute Music' to search the internet,
download music and edit the point-song list.

